  "id": "pavlovian-conditioning",
  "term": "Pavlovian conditioning",
  "definition": "Pavlovian conditioning is a form of classical conditioning in which different stimuli are presented close together in time, so a response becomes linked to a stimulus even though the response has no rewarding or punishing consequence. The term comes from Pavlov’s experiments in which dogs learned to salivate to a tone.",
